                <pb facs="0204" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862 20210/1221: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-02T20:00:00-03:00">April 2, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1139. Aranha says that the Director of Posts and Telegraph has ascertained that
                    certain Axis agents here are carrying on secret communications with Axis agents
                    in Argentina and that he is taking steps to check communications. He said that
                    the Brazilian Government would cut the Italcable (Italian Government owned)
                    between Rio de Janeiro, Buenos Aires, because the Brazilian Government suspects
                    that the company is cooperating with the agents in transmitting clandestine
                    messages.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
